## What problem(s) does this PR solve?

Two things:
- Simplify. The old code is super verbose and hard to read.
- Prepare for https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12224. This one is a little hard to see, but the gist is "make it more maintainable".

## Additional information

The old code basically converted keys and values into temporary arrays, trying to do the same thing as the `Array` implementation. This made it hard to read and slow.
The new code just iterates once and shortcuts in-loop if no conversion is needed.

Also adds a check to make sure no keys overlap after converting to the target type, rejecting `assign` if yes.

### Benchmarks

The speed is around the same as before (+- 10%).

The performance gap in the regression path probably comes from `validate` needing a copy before validating in-place. A future PR could optimize that which should bring it beyond today's performance.

> Note: Benchmarks were written by AI.

